.TH FUSETEX 1 "October 2026" "Fuse" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fusetex \- evaluate FuseTex source and write a PNG image
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fusetex
[\fB--width\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB--height\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB--seed\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB--preview-line\fR \fIN\fR]
.br
.B fusetex
[\fB--builtins\fR]
.br
.B fusetex lsp
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fusetex
reads one FuseTex program from standard input and writes a PNG image to
standard output. The final program result must be a \fBvec4\fR. Intermediate
preview lines may produce a scalar or vector value and are visualized by the
renderer.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B lsp
Run the capability language server over JSON-RPC on standard input and output.
It provides diagnostics, receiver-aware completion, and hover documentation.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --width " N"
Set the output width in pixels. The default is 256.
.TP
.BI --height " N"
Set the output height in pixels. The default is 256.
.TP
.BI --seed " N"
Set the deterministic seed used by \fBnoise\fR. The default is 0.
.TP
.BI --preview-line " N"
Render the intermediate result selected by source line \fIN\fR.
.TP
.B --builtins
Print all FuseTex function signatures, globals, and their descriptions.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Print a short usage guide.
.SH LANGUAGE API
FuseTex uses dot calls for pipeline stages. The value on the left is passed as
the first argument to the next function.
.PP
.nf
center(vec2) -> vec2       aspect(vec2) -> vec2
add(float, float) -> float
add(vec2, vec2) -> vec2
multiply(float, float) -> float
multiply(vec2, float) -> vec2
sin(float) -> float         cos(float) -> float
abs(float) -> float         floor(float) -> float
fract(float) -> float       length(vec2) -> float
dot(vec2, vec2) -> float
smoothstep(float, float, float) -> float
noise(vec2) -> float
noise(vec2, vec2) -> float
vec2(float, float) -> vec2
vec3(float, float, float) -> vec3
vec4(vec2, float, float) -> vec4
vec4(vec3, float) -> vec4
vec4(float, float, float, float) -> vec4
rgb(float, float, float) -> vec3
colorize(float, vec3) -> vec4
.fi
.PP
.B uv
is the normalized coordinate of the current texture pixel.
\fBresolution\fR is the output size in pixels.
.PP
\fBnoise\fR generates seeded improved Perlin noise in the [0, 1] range. Its
optional second argument is a period in noise-coordinate units and makes the
result tileable.
.PP
Use \fBfusetex --builtins\fR for the complete descriptions of these functions.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
fusetex < texture.ptex > texture.png
fusetex --width 512 --height 256 < texture.ptex > texture.png
fusetex --seed 42 --preview-line 3 < texture.ptex > preview.png
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns zero on success and non-zero for invalid options, source, rendering,
or output errors.
